; When the xact command copies a posting from history and gives it a new
; amount, nothing that described the old amount survives: not the
; calculated flag (which hides the amount in print), not a balance
; assertion, and not the history's lot annotation on a bare amount.

2024/01/01 Lunch
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Dinner
    Expenses:Food    $20.00
    Assets:Bank    $-20.00 = $-20.00

; The price keeps the journal valued in one commodity, which the
; ValuationFooting test (test/semantic/footing.py) requires of every journal
; it replays under `bal -V --unrealized`.
P 2023/12/01 AAPL $2.00

2024/01/03 Snack
    Expenses:Food    5 AAPL {$2.00} [2023/12/01]
    Assets:Cash

; The history's Cash amount was calculated; the drafted one is given.
test xact 2024/03/01 Lunch to Assets:Cash '$-7' Expenses:Food
2024/03/01 Lunch
    Assets:Cash                               $-7.00
    Expenses:Food
end test

; The history's assertion = $-20.00 described the old amount.
test xact 2024/03/01 Dinner to Assets:Bank '$-7' Expenses:Food
2024/03/01 Dinner
    Assets:Bank                               $-7.00
    Expenses:Food
end test

; A bare amount takes the commodity, not the history's lot.
test xact 2024/03/01 Snack to Expenses:Food 3 Assets:Cash
2024/03/01 Snack
    Expenses:Food                             3 AAPL
    Assets:Cash
end test

; A cost with no amount keeps the history's quantity, but the cost names a
; new lot: the history's user-written lot does not survive beside it.
test xact 2024/03/01 Snack to Expenses:Food '@' '$3.00' Assets:Cash
2024/03/01 Snack
    Expenses:Food                             5 AAPL @ $3.00
    Assets:Cash
end test
